### 5. Conclusion
The **Sandboxed** project successfully demonstrates practical Operating Systems concepts by unifying modern Linux kernel isolation primitives into a secure, observable, and measurable platform. 

By utilizing unprivileged user namespaces and bubblewrap alongside delegated cgroups v2 controllers, it proves that robust multi-tenant program execution can be achieved without the security attack surface of privileged Docker daemons or the heavy boot latency of virtual machines. 

The system successfully enforces hardware boundaries against memory leaks, CPU starvation, and fork-bombs, while strictly restricting filesystem access and network egress. It provides a reliable software engineering foundation for academic evaluation, automated grading, and secure sandbox experimentation.

---

